WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.794 --> 00:00:09.616
The next day Matt needed to talk to Dede as soon as possible. He found her

2
00:00:09.617 --> 00:00:14.461
at her locker before homeroom started. "I'm quitting La Bohème !" he announced dramatically. "Why would you

3
00:00:14.462 --> 00:00:23.367
do that? Are you sick or something?" Dede blinked, as if she couldn't believe what she

4
00:00:23.368 --> 00:00:30.257
was hearing. "No, I'm fine. I just don't want to do it anymore. It's too hard."

5
00:00:30.258 --> 00:00:39.503
"You get to sing with a major opera company, and you want to quit just because it's

6
00:00:39.504 --> 00:00:43.596
hard?" Dede shook her head. "Of course it's hard. It's opera!" It was Matt's turn to

7
00:00:43.597 --> 00:00:54.401
be surprised. "You've hardly said a word to me since I got the part. I thought

8
00:00:54.402 --> 00:01:06.977
you'd be happy I'm quitting." "Happy? I'm horrified!" "Fine. I don't care what you think anyway," Matt

9
00:01:06.978 --> 00:01:10.656
said angrily, and he started to walk away. He'd expected Dede to be more sympathetic. "Wait!

10
00:01:10.657 --> 00:01:19.400
Let me explain." Matt turned around and leaned on the locker next to Dede's. "Look, I

11
00:01:19.401 --> 00:01:28.302
admit I was jealous when you got the part. I thought either we'd both get into the

12
00:01:28.303 --> 00:01:38.717
chorus, or we'd both be rejected. I was really down on myself for failing. But then

13
00:01:38.718 --> 00:01:43.634
Mrs. Menendez explained that they'd had a lot of girls try out, and they needed more

14
00:01:43.635 --> 00:01:52.103
guys, so . . ." "So you're saying I only got a part because I'm a guy?"

15
00:01:52.104 --> 00:01:58.364
"No! You're an awesome singer! I'm saying that knowing they needed boys helped me to get

16
00:01:58.365 --> 00:02:11.266
over my rejection. Besides, I've got some other stuff going on right now. I don't have

17
00:02:11.267 --> 00:02:21.856
time to do everything." "Oh." Matt stared at his shoes. For the past few weeks, he'd been

18
00:02:21.857 --> 00:02:29.174
so busy thinking about himself that he hadn't stopped to consider how Dede might be feeling.

19
00:02:29.175 --> 00:02:34.236
"I know it must be hard sometimes, but you can't throw away an amazing opportunity. Now

20
00:02:34.237 --> 00:02:42.816
tell me why you want to quit the opera." "Yes, do tell us!" some familiar voices said

21
00:02:42.817 --> 00:02:48.903
from behind Matt. He turned around to find Tyler and Brian grinning at him. "Mi-mi-mi-mi-mi. I'm

22
00:02:48.904 --> 00:02:57.221
a famous opera star," Tyler sang. "But I don't want to be a star!" Brian sang.

23
00:02:57.222 --> 00:03:04.141
"Oh, this is tragic!" Tyler sang, touching the back of his hand to his forehead. "Tragic," Brian

24
00:03:04.142 --> 00:03:14.549
echoed. "What will I do?" "Stop it right now!" Dede was furious. "You guys don't realize

25
00:03:14.550 --> 00:03:19.372
how good Matt is, how much talent he has. I don't know why he's friends with

26
00:03:19.373 --> 00:03:27.953
people who don't appreciate him!" The bell rang for the start of homeroom, and Dede stormed off.

27
00:03:27.954 --> 00:03:35.126
"Whoa!" Tyler said. "She must really like you, Matt. Who was that?" "A friend. A real

28
00:03:35.127 --> 00:03:52.177
friend." Matt reached into his backpack and tossed a book at Tyler. "Here, you left this

29
00:03:52.178 --> 00:03:57.587
at my house." Then he ran after Dede. "You really don't know who she is, do you?"

30
00:03:57.588 --> 00:04:09.750
Brian said to Tyler. "She's that pitcher I was telling you about. My sister's on the

31
00:04:09.751 --> 00:04:14.262
high school softball team, and that girl Dede is so good that she practices with them

32
00:04:14.263 --> 00:04:26.004
sometimes." "You're talking about the player with the killer fastball, right?" "Yeah, that's the one, and now

33
00:04:26.005 --> 00:04:31.146
she's defending Matt. Did you also notice that he threw that book with his left arm?

34
00:04:31.147 --> 00:04:38.486
The one with the bad elbow? Dude, I think our man has been doing opera for

35
00:04:38.487 --> 00:04:47.712
a long time." "Whoa!" Tyler said again as he watched Matt catch up with Dede. ***

36
00:04:47.713 --> 00:04:54.059
Matt was not looking forward to his next rehearsal. Ever since the last one, he'd been arguing

37
00:04:54.060 --> 00:05:01.545
with his mother about quitting. She finally agreed that he could, but only if he told

38
00:05:01.546 --> 00:05:08.369
the director in person. As Matt walked into the theater, he practiced his speech under his

39
00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:16.376
breath. He'd get this over quickly and then he'd text his mom at the café where she

40
00:05:16.377 --> 00:05:25.290
was waiting. "Hey, urchin!" a soft voice called as Matt walked down the aisle. He turned

41
00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:33.855
around and was startled to see the singer who played Mimi. His words came tumbling out.

42
00:05:33.856 --> 00:05:43.357
"Oh! Were you talking to me? I'm so sorry I bumped into you last rehearsal. I didn't

43
00:05:43.358 --> 00:05:53.178
mean to. I was only trying—" Mimi laughed. "I'm fine. I just wanted to check how

44
00:05:53.179 --> 00:06:00.987
you're doing. Don't let Bob get to you." Matt looked confused. "Bob?" "Mr. Berman. He yells

45
00:06:00.988 --> 00:06:08.001
at everybody. He's a director, and that's what directors do. If you're going to be an opera

46
00:06:08.002 --> 00:06:14.564
singer, you have to get used to directors yelling. Now tell me you're okay." Mimi smiled

47
00:06:14.565 --> 00:06:25.051
kindly at Matt, and he smiled back. "I'm okay." As the opera star walked away, Tim

48
00:06:25.052 --> 00:06:30.638
came up to Matt. "She spoke to you!" Tim said in amazement. "She has an unbelievable voice,

49
00:06:30.639 --> 00:06:33.972
and she's so pretty, and . . ." His voice trailed off as he watched Mimi

50
00:06:33.973 --> 00:06:42.452
talking to the director. "And you have a crush on her!" Tim laughed and gave Matt

51
00:06:42.453 --> 00:06:55.108
a little punch on the arm. "So why'd you run off the other day?" "I didn't run

52
00:06:55.109 --> 00:07:01.107
off. I—" But before Matt could explain, Mr. Berman was calling them all to gather round.

53
00:07:01.108 --> 00:07:05.533
"We have a special guest performer today!" he announced with a flourish. "Nigel the horse will

54
00:07:05.534 --> 00:07:12.612
be pulling Musetta's carriage. Now let's try to get through the entire act with no stopping. Is

55
00:07:12.613 --> 00:07:23.916
everybody ready?" "A real horse?" Matt raised his eyebrows at Tim. "When I saw The Barber

56
00:07:23.917 --> 00:07:28.757
of Seville , two guys in a costume played the dancing donkey." "Let's hope this horse

57
00:07:28.758 --> 00:07:51.502
doesn't have to dance." Matt took his place offstage. As the orchestra played the opening notes, he

58
00:07:51.503 --> 00:07:55.827
realized that he liked this strange world that combined singing and drama and even an occasional

59
00:07:55.828 --> 00:08:06.658
live animal. He couldn't wait to try on his costume later that day. When he heard

60
00:08:06.659 --> 00:08:14.383
his cue, Matt ran onstage without bumping into anyone. He sang every note perfectly. The act was

61
00:08:14.384 --> 00:08:25.809
going so well, he couldn't understand why the director was suddenly shouting for them all to

62
00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:30.118
stop. Then people started laughing, and Matt realized the horse had pooped right in the middle

63
00:08:30.119 --> 00:08:36.863
of the stage. "Stagehands!" the director yelled. Mimi winked at Matt. "I guess you're not the worst

64
00:08:36.864 --> 00:08:45.186
performer today." Matt laughed. As the stagehands cleaned up the mess, he realized something else. He

65
00:08:45.187 --> 00:08:54.696
liked singing and he was good at it. He'd made some new friends here, and he

66
00:08:54.697 --> 00:08:58.005
didn't care what his friends at school thought. He wasn't going to give up opera. "I'll show

67
00:08:58.006 --> 00:09:11.198
them," he thought. Then he realized that he really could show them. "I'll give them tickets!"

